// 32_gpu_compute.zp
// Z+ submits compute work through CHAIN_MDE with prefer_gpu=true.
//
// trigger fires (42). compute.run(double, prefer_gpu = true) submits
// the work through CHAIN_MDE; device_select asks the gpu_compute
// registry for a backend. If a GPU backend (e.g. virtio-virgl) is
// registered AND can_dispatch returns 1, that backend wins. Otherwise
// CPU handles it (CPU backend is always at registry index 0).
//
// Today the virtio-virgl backend's dispatch is a CPU-fallback path
// that logs "[gpu] dispatch routed to virtio-virgl (CPU fallback --
// no shader compiler yet)". Real shader execution lands when
// docs/GPU_HOLES.md D1-D3 (compiler integration) closes; the rest of
// this Z+ program does not change.

trigger : emit(42)
double  : input -> multiply(2) -> output
runner  : input -> compute.run(double, prefer_gpu = true)
log     : input -> tap.log

trigger -> runner -> log

chain compute_demo { trigger runner log }
